WEBVTT

NOTE Prospect discovery — Loopr — Riverstone Couriers
NOTE Interviewer: Priya Shah (PM). Prospect: Kenji Okafor, Founder/Operator.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:13.220
<v Priya>Kenji, thanks for taking the call. I know you're running ops single-handed so I'll keep this tight.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:25.450
<v Kenji>Appreciate that. Yeah, look, I've been using a spreadsheet and a whiteboard for two years. I know it doesn't scale but I also know what I can afford, which is approximately nothing.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:36.180
<v Priya>Fair. Walk me through a typical morning — where does the spreadsheet break down?

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:51.330
<v Kenji>Onboarding new drivers, mostly. Every time I hire someone I spend a full day teaching them my spreadsheet conventions. It's a mess. The friction is real, I'm not pretending it isn't.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:01:04.270
<v Priya>So onboarding friction is a top issue for you too. We hear that a lot. What about routing — are you optimizing routes manually?

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:18.940
<v Kenji>Manually, in my head, while drinking coffee. Which works for ten drivers. It won't work for twenty-five. That's why I'm even on this call.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:29.720
<v Priya>Got it. Let me ask about pricing directly — what's your budget reality for a tool like this?

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:48.560
<v Kenji>I'll be blunt. Free is the only acceptable price. If you charge per seat, even five dollars a seat, we won't adopt. My margin is razor-thin and every per-seat tool is a tax I can't pay.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:02:01.880
<v Priya>That's a strong position. So a $50/seat enterprise tier — that's a non-starter for you?

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:18.640
<v Kenji>Fifty bucks a seat? For twenty-five drivers? That's fifteen hundred a month. I make less than that in profit some months. Absolutely not. If that's your model I'll stay on the spreadsheet forever.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:31.420
<v Priya>What would make commercial sense for you? Usage-based? Flat fee? Free with paid add-ons?

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:46.330
<v Kenji>Free tier with a paid upgrade if I grow past a threshold. Like a real free tier, not a fourteen-day trial. If I can run the business on the free tier and you only charge me when I cross fifty drivers, I'll evangelize you.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:55.110
<v Priya>Understood. So the path for you is free-forever-up-to-a-point, not seat-based at all.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:03:08.760
<v Kenji>Correct. Per-seat pricing is dead to me. Charge me for outcomes or scale, not for chairs. And fix the onboarding for new drivers and I'm a customer the day you ship a free tier.
